+"""AOCL-BLIS / LPGEMM vendor provider binding for the U2a matmul slice.
+
+Scope (frozen by ``docs/20-planning/0008-...`` section 7 / the U2a dispatch):
+
+* ``vendor:aocl-lpgemm-bf16`` -- ``aocl_gemm_bf16bf16f32obf16`` with B
+  pre-reordered by ``aocl_reorder_bf16bf16f32of32``; pack happens **outside**
+  the timed GEMM region (Q8 ``aocl_bf16_packed`` protocol);
+* ``vendor:aocl-lpgemm-f32`` -- CBLAS ``cblas_sgemm`` row-major; BLIS packs
+  internally, so pack is **inside** the timed region (Q8 timing level).
+
+Deliberately **not** in scope: int8 / W8A8 (U2b, waits for the M2 contract),
+batched matmul (rank must be 2), strided views, epilogues/biases.
+
+The library is the Q8 ``vendor-gemm-survey`` artifact: BLIS tag 5.3.2,
+explicit ``zen4`` config, ``--disable-blis-arch-type``, ``--int-size=64`` /
+``--blas-int-size=32``, OpenMP threading.  The probe verifies the pinned
+sha256, the BLIS version/commit, the ABI widths and the runtime
+``bli_arch_query_id``/``bli_arch_string`` before a provider can become
+``available``; any failure is a structured ``unavailable`` with a reason, never
+a silent fallback.
+
+Threading is pinned per plan through ``bli_thread_set_num_threads`` and
+verified with ``bli_thread_get_num_threads``; the probe records the default
+thread count and the environment knobs as platform facts.
+"""
